# The addon block below (Core..Widgets, Games\*, Settings..Launcher) is
# grouping only: every file's file scope defines things on PG and the wiring
# happens at ADDON_LOADED, so reordering cannot break it (SPEC.md 10d).
#
# THE IdleBattle\ BLOCK IS THE OPPOSITE: IT IS DEPENDENCY ORDER AND MOVING A
# LINE BREAKS THE ADDON AT LOGIN. Every engine file resolves its imports at
# FILE SCOPE through the IB_SIM_MODULES global:
#     local Hash = IB_SIM_MODULES and IB_SIM_MODULES.Hash or require("sim.Hash")
# WoW has no require(), so that right-hand branch is a nil-call error rather
# than a fallback. Loader.lua creates IB_SIM_MODULES and must load first; each
# engine file then registers itself (its tail) and must load after every file
# it names: Rules names Hash; Sim names Hash, Rand, Mods; Wire names Rules,
# Hash; Snap names Hash; Net names Rules, Sim, Hash, Wire, Snap.
# dev/idlebattle/tools/syncaddon.sh executes this exact order headless with
# require() disabled and goes red if it stops loading -- run it (and --check)
# after touching this block.
#
# The engine files are BYTE-IDENTICAL copies of dev/idlebattle/'s sim/ and
# net/ trees, synced by syncaddon.sh; HandLog.lua is generated by it. Edit the
# HEADLESS ORIGINALS, never these copies (IdleBattle\README.md).

Core.lua
Util.lua
Theme.lua
Comm.lua
Ledger.lua
Widgets.lua
IdleBattle\Loader.lua
IdleBattle\sim\Hash.lua
IdleBattle\sim\Rand.lua
IdleBattle\sim\Mods.lua
IdleBattle\sim\Rules.lua
IdleBattle\sim\Sim.lua
IdleBattle\net\Wire.lua
IdleBattle\net\Snap.lua
IdleBattle\net\Net.lua
IdleBattle\HandLog.lua
